{"step_index":1197,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T20:24:55Z","content":"The project currently has no `.env` at all and doesn't read one yet. Here's everything you need to know:\n\n---\n\n## `.env` File — Your Options\n\n### Option 1: Your project doesn't need one right now\n\nCurrently the paths are **hardcoded** in the app:\n- `D:\\acceleration\\Model_1.csv` etc.\n- `D:\\acceleration\\best.pt`\n- `C:\\Users\\win-10\\Downloads\\3000Samplesv3.mat`\n\nThe app works without any `.env`.\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Create one (recommended for cleanliness)\n\nA `.env` lets you move those hardcoded paths to one config file. Here's how:\n\n**Step 1 — Create the file:**\n```powershell\n# Run this in the neurax_app folder\nNew-Item -Path \"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\.env\" -ItemType File\n```\n\nOr just create it manually in VS Code / Notepad — name it exactly `.env` (no extension).\n\n**Step 2 — Add your config values:**\n```env\n# Model data paths\nMODEL_DIR=D:/acceleration\nMATLAB_MAT=C:/Users/win-10/Downloads/3000Samplesv3.mat\nYOLO_WEIGHTS=D:/acceleration/best.pt\n\n# Financial defaults\nPRICE_PER_UNIT=15.0\nSCRAP_COST=2.5\nOVERHEAD=4.0\n```\n\n**Step 3 — Install `python-dotenv`:**\n```powershell\npip install python-dotenv\n```\n\n**Step 4 — Load it in `app.py`** (top of the file):\n```python\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nload_dotenv()\n\nMODEL_DIR = os.getenv(\"MODEL_DIR\", \"D:/acceleration\")\nYOLO_WEIGHTS = os.getenv(\"YOLO_WEIGHTS\", \"D:/acceleration/best.pt\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### Which one should you do?\n\n| Situation | Recommendation |\n|---|---|\n| Running only on your PC | Don't bother, it works as-is |\n| Sharing with a teammate | Create `.env` so they can set their own paths |\n| Deploying to a server | Definitely use `.env` |\n\nWant me to wire up `.env` support into the app so all paths are configurable from one file?"}
