{"step_index":1237,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T20:29:16Z","content":"Everything compiles clean. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n---\n\n## What was created\n\n### `.env` — your actual config (never commit this)\nLives at `neurax_app/.env`. Contains all your real paths + tunable defaults.\n\n### `.env.example` — safe to commit to Git/show judges\nGeneric placeholder version. Judges see this and understand your app is properly configurable.\n\n### What env vars control now:\n\n| Variable | What it affects |\n|---|---|\n| `MODEL_1/2/3_PATH` | Auto-loader finds your Arena CSV files |\n| `MODEL_DIR` | Fallback folder for all 3 models |\n| `YOLO_WEIGHTS_PATH` | Pre-fills the weights path field in the sidebar |\n| `DEFAULT_SCRAP_COST` | Slider starting value |\n| `DEFAULT_DOWNTIME_COST` | Slider starting value |\n| `DEFAULT_REVENUE_MULTIPLIER` | Slider starting value |\n| `CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` | UNCERTAIN detection cutoff |\n| `NOVEL_THRESHOLD` | NOVEL detection cutoff |\n| `DEBUG` | Verbose logging toggle |\n\n---\n\n### Why judges like this\n\n- **No hardcoded paths** — anyone can run it by editing one file\n- **Separation of config from code** — shows engineering maturity\n- **`.env.example` in the repo** — shows you know what should and shouldn't be committed\n- **Graceful fallback** — if `python-dotenv` isn't installed, the app still works with hardcoded defaults (no crash)"}
